  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 5,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.137,
            0.046,
            0.346,
            0.063
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.087,
            0.847,
            0.162
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 6:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " When Neelima was 3 years old, her mother’s age was 10 times her age. What is the ratio of Neelima’s age to her mother’s age? What would be the ratio of their ages when Neelima is 12 years old? Would it remain the same?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.166,
            0.848,
            0.221
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The ratio of Neelima’s age to her mother’s age when Neelima is 3 years old is 3 : 30 (her mother’s age is 10 times Neelima’s age). In the simplest form, it is 1 : 10."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.221,
            0.847,
            0.277
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When Neelima is 12 years old (i.e., 9 years later), the ratio of their ages will be 12 : 39 (9 years later, her mother would be 39 years old). In the simplest form, it is 4 : 13."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.277,
            0.847,
            0.316
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When we add (or subtract) the same number from the terms of a ratio, the ratio changes and is not necessarily proportional to the original ratio."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.325,
            0.847,
            0.365
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？proportional to 14 : 21."
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.374,
            0.697,
            0.394
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ": 42 6 : _ 2 : _"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.398,
            0.682,
            0.493
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the first ratio, we don’t know the first term. But the second term is 42. It is 2 times the second term of the ratio 14 : 21. So, the first term should also be 2 times 14 (the first term). Hence the proportional ratio is 28 : 42. For the second ratio, the first term is 6."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.496,
            0.679,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What factor should we multiply 14 by to get 6? Can it be an integer? Or should it be a fraction?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.704,
            0.384,
            0.899,
            0.525
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.704,
                0.384,
                0.899,
                0.525
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_5_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.539,
            0.567,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can model this as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "14y = 6.50, y = \\frac{6}{14} = \\frac{3}{7}."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.565,
            0.847,
            0.607
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, we need to multiply 21 (the second term of 14 : 21) also by the same factor "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\frac { 3 } { 7 } } ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.61,
            0.446,
            0.633
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 1 \\times { \\frac { 3 } { 7 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is 9. So, the ratio is 6 : 9."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.636,
            0.498,
            0.654
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the third ratio, the first term is 2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.654,
            0.846,
            0.691
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We can see that when we divide 14 (the first term of 14 : 21) by 7 (HCF of 14 and 21) we get 2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.691,
            0.674,
            0.711
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If we divide 21 also by 7, we get 3. So, the ratio is 2 : 3."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.722,
            0.294,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Filter Coffee!"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.745,
            0.659,
            0.82
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Filter coffee is a beverage made by mixing coffee decoction with milk. Manjunath usually mixes 15 mL of coffee decoction with 35 mL of milk to make one cup of filter coffee in his coffee shop."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.82,
            0.658,
            0.856
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In this case, we can say that the ratio of coffee decoction to milk is 15 : 35."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.856,
            0.661,
            0.912
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If customers want ‘stronger’ filter coffee, Manjunath mixes 20 mL of decoction with 30 mL of milk. The ratio here is 20 : 30."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
